<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kesselsdorf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1745</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-silesian-war">Second Silesian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kesselsdorf was fought on 15 December 1745 west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-silesian-war">Second Silesian War</a>. A Prussian army under Leopold I of Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau">Dessau</a> defeated a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> army supported by Austrian troops, and Dresden was occupied soon after. The defeat forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> to accept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-dresden-1745">Peace of Dresden</a> on 25 December, confirming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>'s possession of Silesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kesselsdorf.jpg" alt="Battle of Kesselsdorf" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brück &amp;amp; Sohn Kunstverlag Meißen · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:01679-Kesselsdorf-1901-Schlacht_bei_Kesselsdorf-Br%C3%BCck_%26_Sohn_Kunstverlag.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
